# Rails Development Rules Index

Development standards live in `.cursor/rules/`. Layer rules load automatically when you edit matching files.

## Always-on

| Rule | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `development-principles` | TDD, simplicity, surgical changes, architecture principles |
| `git-commits` | Conventional Commits for commit messages and pull request titles |

## Layer rules (path-scoped)

| Rule | Applies to |
|------|------------|
| `models` | `app/models/`, `spec/models/`, `spec/factories/` |
| `controllers` | `app/controllers/`, `spec/requests/` |
| `services` | `app/services/`, `spec/services/` |
| `queries` | `app/queries/`, `spec/queries/` |
| `policies` | `app/policies/`, `spec/policies/` |
| `jobs` | `app/jobs/`, `spec/jobs/` |
| `mailers` | `app/mailers/`, mailer views, `spec/mailers/` |
| `migrations` | `db/migrate/`, `db/schema.rb` |
| `views` | `app/views/`, `app/components/`, `app/presenters/` |
| `testing` | `spec/**` (RSpec + Better Specs) |
| `anti-patterns` | `app/**/*.rb`, `spec/**/*.rb` |

## Topic rules

| Rule | Applies to |
|------|------------|
| `ruby-code-style` | `**/*.rb` |
| `rails-database-performance` | `app/models/`, `db/` |
| `rails-security` | `app/controllers/`, `app/policies/` |
| `hotwire-frontend` | `app/views/`, `app/assets/` |
| `javascript-rails` | `app/javascript/` |

## Skills (on-demand workflows)

| Skill | When to use |
|-------|-------------|
| `implement` | Implement a GitHub issue (rules-first → plan → RSpec TDD → Playwright E2E) |
| `code-review-rails` | PR/code review with optional fix workflow |
| `browser-verify-changes` | Manual browser QA of UI changes |
| `rails-schema-via-migrations` | Never hand-edit `db/schema.rb`; update only via Docker migrations |

## Project ops

Docker-only CLI, Playwright E2E, and agent workflow → `AGENTS.md`.

Reference rules in chat with `@rule-name` (e.g. `@models`, `@services`).
